.TH geectl-service-trigger 1  "geectl-service-trigger 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-service\-trigger \- Trigger a server\-side run of a package\*(Aqs services. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the trigger. The trigger only queues the run: the server runs the services asynchronously, so a successful trigger says the run was queued. Check the outcome with `service state`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl service trigger\fR [\fB\-\-service\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trigger a server\-side run of a package\*(Aqs services. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the trigger. The trigger only queues the run: the server runs the services asynchronously, so a successful trigger says the run was queued. Check the outcome with `service state`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-service\fR \fI<SERVICE>\fR
The service the trigger is for: it must be defined in the package\*(Aqs `_service`, and the trigger fails closed when it is not. The server runs the whole service set either way; without this flag, every service runs
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to trigger the services of
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
